From f21a3ec6b0196e60073ac233c5c25fcf9b313d79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:02:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] StridedSpan: values of a point with a stride, results of the
 functions of mgis::function

A StridedSpan views values separated by a constant stride, such as the
components of a point of a field stored component by component, or
point by point with a padding. It has no data method, so that it is
never mapped as contiguous values, and it is not assignable, so that the
algorithms assigning the values of a point can't silently rebind a view.

The functions and evaluators of mgis::function may return a strided
span. The tensor and quantity views and modifiers map it without copy
with tfel::math::StridedCoalescedView (MGIS/Function/TFEL/MapValues.hxx),
and assign_value copies values to and from strided spans. A function
type can then serve both layouts with a single implementation: the
results are identical to the bit (StridedSpanTest).
