 stress, can be viewed as a quantity or as a scalar. `getDataPointer`
 can be overloaded to support other result types.
 
+A function or an evaluator may also return the values of a point as a
+strided span (`mgis::StridedSpan`): `size()` values separated by a
+constant stride, `getPointer()[i * getStride()]` being the `i`-th one.
+This is the natural result of a function whose values are stored
+component by component, or point by point with a padding: the same
+function type then serves both layouts. A strided span has no `data`
+method, so that it is never mapped as contiguous values: the tensor and
+quantity views and modifiers map it with a view having a stride
+(`tfel::math::StridedCoalescedView`), without copy, and the results are
+identical to the bit to the ones obtained from contiguous values. The
+fixed-size views described below require contiguous values. A strided
+span is not assignable: the algorithms assigning the values of a point
+copy them explicitly, so that an assignment can't silently rebind a
+view.
+
